        "sourcePixelsUnmodified": true,
        "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept.\nAsset type: ONE isolated empty outer-jacket reference image for later Meshy image-to-3D generation; a separate wearable game-character garment.\nInput images: Image 1 is the authoritative JACKET DESIGN, COLORS, MATERIAL and ILLUSTRATION STYLE reference: the adult tiger wearing his original outfit. Image 2 is ONLY the wearer's BODY PROPORTIONS and HORIZONTAL T-POSE fit reference. Do not draw either character or the clothing from Image 2.\nPrimary request: Show ONLY the original short OPEN BROWN kimono-like outer jacket as a hollow, unoccupied garment. Preserve the original warm earthy brown fabric, wide dark-edged front lapels and thick hem, short broad loose sleeves, and muted golden-tan/cream turned-back sleeve cuffs. It belongs to the same broad-shouldered, round-bellied, short stocky tiger character, so retain a generously wide, short barrel-shaped torso and roomy armpits rather than a slim human jacket. Open front panels hang apart with space for the large belly; the jacket does not close across the stomach. Keep the design plain and worn-in as in Image 1, with restrained broad fabric folds and slightly scuffed cuff edges; no new ornamentation.\nPose and geometry: the garment is displayed as if its wearer held both arms STRAIGHT HORIZONTALLY out to the sides in a T-pose, matching Image 2. Both empty sleeves extend horizontally from the shoulders with generous shoulder and armpit clearance. Show actual empty sleeve openings with turned-back cuffs, the neck opening, the back fabric visible inside the open front, and believable cloth thickness along the open front edges and lower hem. The jacket is empty and contains NO wearer, mannequin, body, torso, arms, hands, head, fur or undershirt. Do not fill the front opening with a cream shirt or skin. This is ONE complete connected outer jacket, not disconnected sleeve parts.\nStyle/medium: match Image 1's hand-painted anime/game concept illustration with crisp dark ink contours, warm flat colors, restrained cel-shaded volume and a few clear fabric folds. Keep the original brown-and-muted-tan jacket palette. No photorealistic cloth, shiny plastic, metal, armor or sculpted character.\nComposition/framing: a single jacket centered and fully visible, near-front product reference with only a slight three-quarter turn, close to orthographic with very little perspective so both horizontal sleeves and open front are easy to read. Entire cuffs and hem in frame, comfortable even transparent margins. Make the silhouette and empty openings clear. One view only, no turnaround panels or duplicate objects.\nBackground: genuinely transparent RGBA; no floor, ground shadow, scenery, stand, hanger, display mannequin, text, labels, border or watermark.\nAvoid: any character/body part, orange tiger fur, the ivory crossover inner shirt, trousers, boxer briefs, sash, belt, hanging ties, cords, wine bottle, wrist wraps, ankle wraps, accessories, extra garments, closed front, long narrow sleeves, downward arms, slim fitted waist.",
